{"key": "07dd39a3d3b6bdda69dc15f3164990deb52aa574", "outputs": ["```python\nimport re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+(\\.[a-zA-Z]+)+$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+(\\.[a-zA-Z]+)+$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+(\\.[a-zA-Z]+)+$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+(\\.[a-zA-Z]+){2}$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+(\\.[a-zA-Z]+)+$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+(\\.[a-zA-Z]+)*$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```", "```\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+(\\.[a-zA-Z]+)+$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+(\\.[a-zA-Z]+){2}$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+(\\.[a-zA-Z]+){2}$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef match_string(target_string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input string is a valid string with the following format: x.y.z (x, y, z are strings)\n\n    :param target_string: The string to be checked\n    :return: True if the string is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_string('x.y.z')\n    True\n    >>> match_string('x')\n    False\n    '''\n    pattern = r'^[a-zA-Z]+(\\.[a-zA-Z]+)+$'\n    return bool(re.match(pattern, target_string))\n```"]}
{"key": "458e98807a19711d7ecaf098cacb6a8a483ee5fa", "outputs": ["```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    # Create a temporary file in binary mode\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='wb', encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        # Write the results to the temporary file\n        temp_file.write(results.encode('utf-8'))\n        # Return the path of the temporary file\n        return temp_file.name\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='w', encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        temp_file.flush()\n        return temp_file.name\n```", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='w', encoding='utf-8', delete=False) as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        return temp_file.name\n```", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    # Create a temporary file in binary mode\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='wb', encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        # Write the unicode string to the file\n        temp_file.write(results.encode('utf-8'))\n        # Return the path of the temporary file\n        return temp_file.name\n```", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='w', encoding='utf-8', delete=False) as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        return temp_file.name\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    # Create a temporary file in binary mode\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='wb', encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        # Write the results to the file\n        temp_file.write(results.encode('utf-8'))\n        # Return the path of the temporary file\n        return temp_file.name\n```", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='w', encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        return temp_file.name\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='w', encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        temp_file.flush()\n        return temp_file.name\n```", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='w', encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        return temp_file.name\n```", "```python\nimport tempfile\n\ndef write_results(results):\n    '''\n    Create a temporary file with UTF-8 encoding,\n    write the unicode string results to it,\n    and return its path.\n\n    :param results: unicode string\n    :return: path of the temporary file\n    '''\n    with tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile(mode='w', encoding='utf-8') as temp_file:\n        temp_file.write(results)\n        return temp_file.name\n```"]}
{"key": "5d3683f7440800f19368470acd9e7a2041e4074f", "outputs": ["```python\nfrom Crypto.Cipher import AES\n\ndef generate_fingerprint(key, iv):\n    '''\n    Generate a fingerprint for the given key and iv.\n    \n    :param key: The key used for encryption.\n    :param iv: The iv used for encryption.\n    '''\n    cipher = AES.new(key, AES.MODE_CBC, iv)\n    ciphertext = cipher.encrypt(b'')\n    return ciphertext.hex()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom Crypto.Cipher import AES\n\ndef generate_fingerprint(key, iv):\n    '''\n    Generate a fingerprint for the given key and iv.\n    \n    :param key: The key used for encryption.\n    :param iv: The iv used for encryption.\n    '''\n    cipher = AES.new(key, AES.MODE_CBC, iv)\n    ciphertext = cipher.encrypt(b'')\n    return ciphertext.hex()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom Crypto.Cipher import AES\n\ndef generate_fingerprint(key, iv):\n    '''\n    Generate a fingerprint for the given key and iv.\n    \n    :param key: The key used for encryption.\n    :param iv: The iv used for encryption.\n    '''\n    cipher = AES.new(key, AES.MODE_CBC, iv)\n    ciphertext = cipher.encrypt(b'')\n    return ciphertext.hex()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom Crypto.Cipher import AES\n\ndef generate_fingerprint(key, iv):\n    '''\n    Generate a fingerprint for the given key and iv.\n    \n    :param key: The key used for encryption.\n    :param iv: The iv used for encryption.\n    '''\n    # Create an AES cipher object with the provided key and iv\n    cipher = AES.new(key, AES.MODE_CBC, iv)\n    \n    # Encrypt a dummy message to generate a fingerprint\n    dummy_message = b'fingerprint_dummy'\n    encrypted_message = cipher.encrypt(dummy_message)\n    \n    # Return the fingerprint as a hexadecimal string\n    return encrypted_message.hex()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom Crypto.Cipher import AES\n\ndef generate_fingerprint(key, iv):\n    '''\n    Generate a fingerprint for the given key and iv.\n    \n    :param key: The key used for encryption.\n    :param iv: The iv used for encryption.\n    '''\n    cipher = AES.new(key, AES.MODE_CBC, iv)\n    encrypted_data = cipher.encrypt(b'')\n    return encrypted_data.hex()\n```<|/assistant|>", "from Crypto.Cipher import AES\n\ndef generate_fingerprint(key, iv):\n    '''\n    Generate a fingerprint for the given key and iv.\n    \n    :param key: The key used for encryption.\n    :param iv: The iv used for encryption.\n    '''\n    cipher = AES.new(key, AES.MODE_CBC, iv)\n    ciphertext = cipher.encrypt(b'')\n    return ciphertext.hex()[:16]  # Return the first 16 bytes of the ciphertext as the fingerprint\n```", "```python\nfrom Crypto.Cipher import AES\n\ndef generate_fingerprint(key, iv):\n    '''\n    Generate a fingerprint for the given key and iv.\n    \n    :param key: The key used for encryption.\n    :param iv: The iv used for encryption.\n    '''\n    cipher = AES.new(key, AES.MODE_CBC, iv)\n    ciphertext = cipher.encrypt(b'')\n    return ciphertext.hex()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom Crypto.Cipher import AES\n\ndef generate_fingerprint(key, iv):\n    '''\n    Generate a fingerprint for the given key and iv.\n    \n    :param key: The key used for encryption.\n    :param iv: The iv used for encryption.\n    '''\n    # Create an AES cipher object\n    cipher = AES.new(key, AES.MODE_CBC, iv)\n    \n    # Encrypt a dummy message to get the fingerprint\n    dummy_message = b'0123456789abcdef'\n    encrypted_message = cipher.encrypt(dummy_message)\n    \n    # Return the fingerprint as a hexadecimal string\n    return encrypted_message.hex()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom Crypto.Cipher import AES\n\ndef generate_fingerprint(key, iv):\n    '''\n    Generate a fingerprint for the given key and iv.\n    \n    :param key: The key used for encryption.\n    :param iv: The iv used for encryption.\n    '''\n    # Create an AES cipher object with the provided key and iv\n    cipher = AES.new(key, AES.MODE_CBC, iv)\n    \n    # Encrypt some dummy data to generate a fingerprint\n    dummy_data = b'0123456789abcdef'\n    encrypted_data = cipher.encrypt(dummy_data)\n    \n    # Return the fingerprint as a hexadecimal string\n    return encrypted_data.hex()\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom Crypto.Cipher import AES\n\ndef generate_fingerprint(key, iv):\n    '''\n    Generate a fingerprint for the given key and iv.\n    \n    :param key: The key used for encryption.\n    :param iv: The iv used for encryption.\n    '''\n    cipher = AES.new(key, AES.MODE_CBC, iv)\n    ciphertext = cipher.encrypt(b'')\n    return ciphertext.hex()\n```<|/assistant|>"]}
{"key": "712d7362b37ffb65f3be61a43c6b7be508bb56f9", "outputs": ["```python\nimport re\n\ndef search(query):\n    '''\n    Check if it contains 'www.example.com/' or 'beta.example.com/'.\n\n    :param query: The query to be checked\n    :return: 'Search results for: <query>' if the query is valid, 'No results found for: <query>' otherwise\n    '''\n    pattern = r'www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/'\n    if re.search(pattern, query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef search(query):\n    '''\n    Check if it contains 'www.example.com/' or 'beta.example.com/'.\n\n    :param query: The query to be checked\n    :return: 'Search results for: <query>' if the query is valid, 'No results found for: <query>' otherwise\n    '''\n    pattern = r'www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/'\n    if re.search(pattern, query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef search(query):\n    '''\n    Check if it contains 'www.example.com/' or 'beta.example.com/'.\n\n    :param query: The query to be checked\n    :return: 'Search results for: <query>' if the query is valid, 'No results found for: <query>' otherwise\n    '''\n    pattern = r'www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/'\n    if re.search(pattern, query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        return f'No results found for: {query}'\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\ndef search(query):\n    '''\n    Check if it contains 'www.example.com/' or 'beta.example.com/'.\n\n    :param query: The query to be checked\n    :return: 'Search results for: <query>' if the query is valid, 'No results found for: <query>' otherwise\n    '''\n    pattern = r'www\\.example\\.com/|beta\\.example\\.com/'\n    if re.search(pattern, query):\n        return f'Search results for: {query}'\n    else:\n        ret