    \n    # Unmarshal the data\n    unmarshalled_data = marshal.loads(byte_data)\n    \n    return unmarshalled_data\n```", "```python\nimport marshal\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/unmarshal')\ndef unmarshal_data():\n    '''\n    Get the marshalled data from the request using 'data' as the key.\n    Unmarshal the data by converting it from hex to bytes,\n    Return the unmarshalled data.\n    '''\n    marshalled_data = request.args.get('data', default=None)\n    if marshalled_data:\n        # Convert hex string to bytes\n        byte_data = bytes.fromhex(marshalled_data)\n        # Unmarshal the data\n        unmarshalled_data = marshal.loads(byte_data)\n        return unmarshalled_data\n    else:\n        return \"No marshalled data provided\", 400\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask route `/unmarshal` that expects a `data` parameter in the query string. It attempts to unmarshal the data from hexadecimal format to bytes and then uses `marshal.loads()` to convert it back into its original form. If no data is provided, it returns an error message with a 400 status code. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport marshal\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/unmarshal')\ndef unmarshal_data():\n    marshalled_data = request.args.get('data', default=None)\n    if marshalled_data is None:\n        return \"No marshalled data provided\", 400\n    \n    # Convert hex string to bytes\n    byte_data = bytes.fromhex(marshalled_data)\n    \n    # Unmarshal the data\n    unmarshalled_data = marshal.loads(byte_data)\n    \n    return unmarshalled_data\n```", "```python\nimport marshal\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/unmarshal')\ndef unmarshal_data():\n    '''\n    Get the marshalled data from the request using 'data' as the key.\n    Unmarshal the data by converting it from hex to bytes,\n    Return the unmarshalled data.\n    '''\n    marshalled_data = request.arg