{"key": "b51807da582b76ad1017f26269215a72a5619537", "outputs": ["```python\nfrom flask import request, send_file, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/download')\ndef download():\n    file_name = request.args.get('file')\n    if not file_name:\n        return \"File name not provided\", 400\n    \n    file_path = f'static/{file_name}'\n    if not app.static_folder or not file_path.startswith(app.static_folder):\n        return \"Invalid file path\", 403\n    \n    try:\n        return send_file(file_path, as_attachment=True)\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        return \"File not found\", 404\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import request, send_file, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/download')\ndef download():\n    # Read the file name from the request\n    file_name = request.args.get('file_name')\n    \n    # Check if the file name is provided\n    if not file_name:\n        return \"File name not provided\", 400\n    \n    # Construct the full path to the file in the static directory\n    file_path = app.static_folder + '/' + file_name\n    \n    # Send the file as an attachment\n    return send_file(file_path, as_attachment=True)\n```", "```python\nfrom flask import request, send_file, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/download')\ndef download():\n    file_name = request.args.get('file_name')\n    if not file_name:\n        return \"File name not provided\", 400\n    \n    file_path = f'static/{file_name}'\n    if not file_path.endswith('.pdf'):\n        return \"Invalid file type\", 400\n    \n    return send_file(file_path, as_attachment=True)\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import request, send_file, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/download')\ndef download():\n    # Read the file name from the request\n    file_name = request.args.get('file_name')\n    \n    # Check if the file name is provided\n    if not file_name:\n        return \"File name not provided\", 400\n    \n    # Construct the full path to the file in the static directory\n    file_path = app.static_folder + '/' + file_name\n    \n    # Send the file as an attachment\n    return send_file(file_path, as_attachment=True)\n```", "```python\nfrom flask import request, send_file, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/download')\ndef download():\n    file_name = request.args.get('file')\n    if not file_name:\n        return \"No file specified\", 400\n    \n    file_path = f'static/{file_name}'\n    if not file_path.endswith('.pdf'):\n        return \"Invalid file type\", 400\n    \n    try:\n        return send_file(file_path, as_attachment=True)\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        return \"File not found\", 404\n```", "```python\nfrom flask import request, send_file, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/download')\ndef download():\n    # Read the file name from the request\n    file_name = request.args.get('file_name')\n    \n    # Check if the file name is provided\n    if not file_name:\n        return \"File name not provided\", 400\n    \n    # Construct the full path to the file in the static directory\n    file_path = app.static_folder + '/' + file_name\n    \n    # Send the file as an attachment\n    return send_file(file_path, as_attachment=True)\n```", "```python\nfrom flask import request, send_file, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/download')\ndef download():\n    # Get the file name from the request\n    file_name = request.args.get('file')\n    \n    # Check if the file exists in the static directory\n    if file_name and file_name.endswith('.txt'):  # Example: only allow .txt files\n        return send_file(f'static/{file_name}', as_attachment=True)\n    else:\n        return \"File not found or invalid format\", 404\n```\n\nThis code defines a route `/download` that accepts a query parameter `file` to specify the file to download. It checks if the file exists in the `static` directory and sends it as an attachment if it does. If the file is not found or has an invalid format, it returns an error message with a status code of 404. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import request, send_file, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/download')\ndef download():\n    file_name = request.args.get('file_name')\n    if not file_name:\n        return \"File name not provided\", 400\n    \n    file_path = f'static/{file_name}'\n    if not file_path.endswith('.pdf'):\n        return \"Invalid file type\", 400\n    \n    return send_file(file_path, as_attachment=True)\n```", "```python\nfrom flask import request, send_file, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/download')\ndef download():\n    # Read the file name from the request\n    file_name = request.args.get('file')\n    \n    # Check if the file exists in the static directory\n    if file_name and os.path.exists(os.path.join(app.static_folder, file_name)):\n        # Send the file as an attachment\n        return send_file(file_name, as_attachment=True)\n    else:\n        # Return a 404 error if the file does not exist\n        return \"File not found\", 404\n```\n\nNote: This code assumes that the files are stored in the `static` folder of your Flask application. If your files are stored elsewhere, you will need to adjust the path accordingly. Additionally, this code uses the `os` module to check if the file exists, so make sure to import it at the beginning of your script. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import request, send_file, Flask\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/download')\ndef download():\n    file_name = request.args.get('file')\n    if not file_name:\n        return \"File name not provided\", 400\n    \n    file_path = f'static/{file_name}'\n    if not file_path.endswith('.pdf'):\n        return \"Invalid file type\", 400\n    \n    return send_file(file_path, as_attachment=True)\n```"]}
{"key": "b5b7fed2f34db06cfa2c8bf6282fffaf329565c0", "outputs": ["```python\n    target_url = request.args.get('target_url')\n\n    if not target_url:\n        return \"No target URL provided\", 400\n\n    # Check if the target URL is internal (same domain)\n    if target_url.startswith(request.host_url):\n        return redirect(target_url), 302\n    else:\n        return \"External URLs are not allowed\", 403\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    target_url = request.args.get('target_url')\n\n    if target_url and target_url.startswith('http://') or target_url.startswith('https://'):\n        return redirect(target_url), 302\n\n    return \"Invalid target URL\", 400\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    target_url = request.args.get('target_url')\n    if not target_url or 'http://' in target_url or 'https://' in target_url:\n        return redirect('/error'), 400\n\n    return redirect(target_url), 302\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    target_url = request.args.get('target_url')\n\n    if not target_url or 'http://' in target_url or 'https://' in target_url:\n        return redirect('/error'), 400\n\n    return redirect(target_url), 302\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    target_url = request.args.get('target_url')\n\n    if not target_url:\n        return \"Target URL not provided\", 400\n\n    # Check if the target URL is within the same domain\n    if not target_url.startswith(request.host_url):\n        return \"Invalid target URL\", 400\n\n    return redirect(target_url), 302\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\n    target_url = request.args.get('target_url')\n\n    if not target_url:\n        return \"Error: No target URL provided\", 400\n\n    # Check if the target URL is internal\n    if target_url.startswith('/'):\n        return redirect(target_url)\n    else:\n        return \"Error: External URLs are not allowed\", 403\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import request, Flask, redirect\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/redirect')\ndef redirect_to():\n    target_url = request.args.get('target_url')\n    \n    if not target_url or 'http://' in target_url or 'https://' in target_url:\n        return redirect('/error'), 400\n    \n    return redirect(target_url), 302\n```", "```python\n    target_url = request.args.get('target_url')\n\n    if not target_url:\n        return \"Error: No target URL provided\", 400\n\n    # Check if the target URL is within the same domain\n    if not target_url.startswith(request.host_url):\n        return \"Error: Target URL must be on the same domain\", 400\n\n    return redirect(target_url)\n```", "```python\n    target_url = request.args.get('target_url')\n    if not target_url or 'http://' in target_url or 'https://' in target_url:\n        return redirect('/error'), 400\n\n    return redirect(target_url), 302\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom flask import request, Flask, redirect\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/redirect')\ndef redirect_to():\n    target_url = request.args.get('target_url')\n    \n    if target_url and target_url.startswith('http://') or target_url.startswith('https://'):\n        return \"Error: Target URL must be internal.\", 400\n    \n    return redirect(target_url), 302\n```\n\nThis code defines a route `/redirect` that takes a `target_url` parameter from the query string. It checks if the target URL is internal (starts with `http://` or `https://`). If it's not internal, it returns an error message with a status code of 400. Otherwise, it redirects the user to the specified target URL using a 302 status code. <|/assistant|>"]}
