ciphertext over the specified channel. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nfrom Crypto.Cipher import AES\nimport base64\n\ndef send_encrypted(secret_key, channel, message):\n    '''\n    Encrypt the message after creating a cipher,\n    and send it over the channel passed as parameter.\n\n    :param secret_key: secret key used for encryption\n    :param channel: channel to send the encrypted message\n    :param message: message to encrypt\n    '''\n    # Ensure the secret key is 16 bytes (AES block size)\n    if len(secret_key) != 16:\n        raise ValueError(\"Secret key must be 16 bytes long\")\n\n    # Create a new AES cipher object\n    cipher = AES.new(secret_key, AES.MODE_EAX)\n\n    # Encrypt the message\n    ciphertext, tag = cipher.encrypt_and_digest(message.encode('utf-8'))\n\n    # Encode the ciphertext and tag in base64 for transmission\n    encoded_ciphertext = base64.b64encode(ciphertext).decode('utf-8')\n    encoded_tag = base64.b64encode(tag).decode('utf-8')\n\n    # Send the encoded ciphertext and tag over the channel\n    channel.send((encoded_ciphertext, encoded_tag))\n```\n\nThis code defines a function `send_encrypted` that takes a secret key, a channel, and a message as input. It uses AES encryption with the EAX mode to encrypt the message. The ciphertext and tag are then encoded in base64 for transmission over the specified channel. <|/assistant|>"]}
{"key": "ca89e6bafa87347fd2cb2011ece1d60cd3bce7ae", "outputs": ["```python\nimport re\n\n\ndef search_pattern(pattern, string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input URL is a valid URL with the following format: (www|beta).example.com/\n\n    :param target_url: The URL to be checked\n    :return: True if the URL is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_url('www.example.com/')\n    True\n    >>> match_url('beta.example.com/')\n    True\n    '''\n    # Define the regular expression pattern\n    url_pattern = r'^(www|beta)\\.example\\.com/$'\n    \n    # Use re.match to check if the string matches the pattern\n    if re.match(url_pattern, string):\n        return True\n    else:\n        return False\n```", "```python\nimport re\n\n\ndef search_pattern(pattern, string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input URL is a valid URL with the following format: (www|beta).example.com/\n\n    :param target_url: The URL to be checked\n    :return: True if the URL is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_url('www.example.com/')\n    True\n    >>> match_url('beta.example.com/')\n    True\n    '''\n    # Define the regular expression pattern\n    url_pattern = r'^(www|beta)\\.example\\.com/$'\n    \n    # Use re.match to check if the string matches the pattern\n    if re.match(url_pattern, string):\n        return True\n    else:\n        return False\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport re\n\n\ndef search_pattern(pattern, string):\n    '''\n    Check if the input URL is a valid URL with the following format: (www|beta).example.com/\n\n    :param target_url: The URL to be checked\n    :return: True if the URL is valid, False otherwise\n\n    >>> match_url('www.example.com/')\n    True\n    >>> match_url('beta.example.com/')\n    True\n    '''\n    # Define the regular expression pattern for the URL\n    url_pattern = r'^(www|beta)\\.example\\.com/$'\n    \n    # Use re.match to check if the string matches the pattern\n    if re.match(url_pattern, string):\n        return True\n    else