{"key": "ddf88072cd9c78dbe23cfc55eaa93d18dd9fe9d5", "outputs": ["```python\nimport os\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/install')\ndef install_package():\n    package_name = request.args.get('package')\n    if not package_name:\n        return \"Package name is required\", 400\n    \n    try:\n        # Assuming conda is installed and accessible in the environment\n        os.system(f\"conda install -y {package_name}\")\n        return f\"{package_name} installed successfully\", 200\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"Failed to install {package_name}: {str(e)}\", 500\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask route `/install` that takes a `package` parameter from the query string. It then attempts to install the specified package using `conda`. If successful, it returns a success message; otherwise, it returns an error message with details about the failure. Note that this assumes `conda` is installed and accessible in the environment where the Flask application is running. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport os\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/install')\ndef install_package():\n    package = request.args.get('package')\n    if not package:\n        return \"Error: Package name is missing\", 400\n    \n    try:\n        # Assuming conda is installed and accessible\n        os.system(f\"conda install -y {package}\")\n        return f\"{package} installed successfully\"\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"Error installing {package}: {str(e)}\", 500\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask route `/install` that takes a package name as a query parameter. It then attempts to install the specified package using `conda`. If successful, it returns a success message; otherwise, it returns an error message with the details of the failure. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport os\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/install')\ndef install_package():\n    package_name = request.args.get('package')\n    if not package_name:\n        return \"Error: Package name is required\", 400\n    \n    try:\n        # Assuming conda is installed and accessible\n        os.system(f\"conda install -y {package_name}\")\n        return f\"{package_name} installed successfully\", 200\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"Error installing {package_name}: {str(e)}\", 500\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask route `/install` that accepts a package name as a query parameter. It uses `os.system` to execute the `conda install` command to install the specified package. If the package is successfully installed, it returns a success message; otherwise, it returns an error message with details about the failure. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport os\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/install')\ndef install_package():\n    package_name = request.args.get('package')\n    if not package_name:\n        return \"Package name is required\", 400\n    \n    try:\n        os.system(f\"conda install -c conda-forge {package_name}\")\n        return f\"{package_name} installed successfully\", 200\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"Failed to install {package_name}: {str(e)}\", 500\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport os\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/install')\ndef install_package():\n    package = request.args.get('package')\n    if not package:\n        return \"No package specified\", 400\n    \n    # Assuming conda is installed and accessible in the system's PATH\n    try:\n        os.system(f\"conda install -y {package}\")\n        return f\"{package} installed successfully\", 200\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"Failed to install {package}: {str(e)}\", 500\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask route `/install` that takes a package name as a query parameter. It uses `os.system` to execute the `conda install` command to install the specified package. If the package is not specified or installation fails, it returns an appropriate error message. <|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport os\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/install')\ndef install_package():\n    package = request.args.get('package')\n    if not package:\n        return \"Package name is required\", 400\n    \n    # Assuming conda is installed and accessible\n    os.system(f\"conda install -y {package}\")\n    \n    return f\"{package} installed successfully\", 200\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport os\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/install')\ndef install_package():\n    '''\n    Get the package from the request using 'package'.\n    Install the package using conda.\n    Return the package name\n    '''\n    package_name = request.args.get('package')\n    \n    if not package_name:\n        return \"Package name is required\", 400\n    \n    try:\n        # Assuming conda is installed and accessible in the PATH\n        os.system(f\"conda install -y {package_name}\")\n        return f\"{package_name} installed successfully\", 200\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"Failed to install {package_name}: {str(e)}\", 500\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport os\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/install')\ndef install_package():\n    package = request.args.get('package')\n    if not package:\n        return \"No package specified\", 400\n    \n    # Assuming conda is installed and accessible\n    conda_command = f\"conda install -y {package}\"\n    \n    try:\n        os.system(conda_command)\n        return f\"{package} installed successfully\", 200\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"Failed to install {package}: {str(e)}\", 500\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport os\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/install')\ndef install_package():\n    package = request.args.get('package')\n    if not package:\n        return \"Package name is required\", 400\n    \n    try:\n        os.system(f\"conda install -y {package}\")\n        return f\"{package} installed successfully\", 200\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"Failed to install {package}: {str(e)}\", 500\n```<|/assistant|>", "```python\nimport os\nfrom flask import Flask, request\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route('/install')\ndef install_package():\n    package = request.args.get('package')\n    if not package:\n        return \"Package name is required\", 400\n    \n    try:\n        # Assuming conda is installed and accessible in the environment\n        os.system(f\"conda install -y {package}\")\n        return f\"{package} installed successfully\", 200\n    except Exception as e:\n        return f\"Failed to install {package}: {str(e)}\", 500\n```\n\nThis code defines a Flask route `/install` that takes a package name as a query parameter. It uses `os.system` to execute the `conda install` command to install the specified package. If the package name is missing or an error occurs during installation, it returns an appropriate error message. <|/assistant|>"]}
